# Myelektra Signal v2 — environment template
#
# Copy to apps/web/.env.local for browser variables and fill in real values.
# The real .env is git-ignored. A committed value here is a defect.
#
# Every key is listed with an empty value. Do not invent placeholder values.
#
# THE VITE_ PREFIX IS A SECURITY BOUNDARY, NOT A NAMING CONVENTION.
# Vite inlines only VITE_-prefixed variables into the browser bundle. An
# unprefixed variable cannot reach the client by accident; a prefixed one can
# never be kept out. Adding a VITE_ variable is a decision to make a value
# public. See docs/07-security/secrets.md (R-SE-1) and
# docs/01-architecture/foundation-plan.md (R-FN-3).

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# BROWSER — set on the Vercel deployment, inlined into the bundle, public
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Supabase project URL. Public.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=

# Supabase anon key. Public by design: row-level security is the access
# control, not this key. It must never be the service-role key — client.ts
# rejects a secret credential at runtime.
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# PayPal public client id, for the browser SDK only.
# Deferred: no PayPal code exists until Phase 7 (OD-PP-1).
VITE_PAYPAL_CLIENT_ID=

# sandbox | live. Chosen per deployment, never per request.
# Deferred: no PayPal code exists until Phase 7 (OD-PP-1).
VITE_PAYPAL_ENV=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SERVER — Supabase Edge Functions / Vault only. NEVER in Vercel, NEVER in the
# bundle, NEVER prefixed with VITE_.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Phase 1B creates no Vault entries, because no consumer for them exists yet.
# Provisioning a credential before its consumer exists is what R-SE-1 forbids.
# These are listed so the browser/server split is explicit and so that nobody
# adds one of them with a VITE_ prefix by accident.
#
#   SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY   -> Edge Functions only (Vault)
#   PAYPAL_CLIENT_SECRET_SANDBOX / PAYPAL_CLIENT_SECRET_LIVE -> Phase 7
#   PAYPAL_WEBHOOK_ID                                        -> Phase 7
#   OPENAI_API_KEY                                           -> Phase 4
#   SEARCH_PROVIDER_API_KEY                                  -> Phase 4
#   EMAIL_PROVIDER_API_KEY                                   -> delivery functions
#   CRON_INVOCATION_SECRET                                   -> Phase 4
#
# Read inside a function, never inlined:
#
#   APP_ENV   local | preview | staging | production
APP_ENV=
